// Rule: [T1553.001] Fake Codex Clickfix - Xattr Tmp Helper Quarantine Clear
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1553.001
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR /
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Campaign hunt for source-observed removal of extended attributes from a staged macOS Mach-O payload.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for xattr tmp helper quarantine clear using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: The endpoint recorded the exact source-observed xattr invocation and requires raw-event, file, lineage and ownership review.
// A match does not prove: A match is an investigation lead; it does not prove AMOS execution, successful C2, credential theft, or attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Fake Codex ClickFix - xattr clearing on staged /tmp/helper
// Classification: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR / Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint process events on macOS
//
// Evidence: Cato CTRL observed the second-stage shell downloading a Mach-O
// payload to /tmp/helper, invoking xattr -c on that file, then chmod +x and
// execution. This query isolates the directly observed anti-quarantine action.
// A match is an investigation lead; it does not prove AMOS execution,
// successful C2, credential theft, or attribution.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName =~ "xattr"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "-c"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "/tmp/helper"
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceId,
    DeviceName,
    ReportId,
    ActionType,
    FileName,
    FolderPath,
    ProcessCommandLine,
    ProcessId,
    AccountName,
    AccountUpn,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessId,
    InitiatingProcessAccountName,
    InitiatingProcessAccountUpn,
    SHA1
| order by Timestamp desc
